    {
      "id": "2b77085e-4d13-4aa0-86dd-b73badffbe70",
      "name": "Read Me First",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -2624,
        48
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 520,
        "height": 1040,
        "content": "## Business card OCR to Gmail draft with team notification\n\nTurns a Google Drive folder of scanned business cards into personalised Gmail **drafts** with a document attached, and reports every card to Slack, Discord or Chatwork.\n\n## What it does\n1. Lists every file in an unprocessed Drive folder\n2. Google Gemini reads company, name, e-mail, phone and address off the card image\n3. A Code node repairs the model output and regex-rescues the e-mail if the JSON is malformed\n4. Cards with a valid address become a Gmail **draft** - never sent automatically - with a PDF attached from Drive\n5. Processed cards are moved to a second Drive folder\n6. Success **and** failure are posted to your chat tool, so no card is silently dropped\n\n## How to set up\n1. Open the **Settings** node. It holds every value you need to change.\n2. Paste the two Drive folder IDs and the file ID of the document you want attached. Leave the attachment empty to send no attachment.\n3. Fill in your e-mail signature fields.\n4. Set `notify_channel` to slack, discord or chatwork, then connect that one credential.\n5. Run once manually, then replace the trigger with a Schedule Trigger.\n\n## Requirements\nGoogle Drive OAuth2, Google Gemini (PaLM) API, Gmail OAuth2, and one of Slack, a Discord webhook, or a Chatwork API token.\n\n## How to customise the workflow\nEdit the prompt in **Extract Card Data with Gemini** to pull extra fields, change the wording in **Build Email Content**, or delete the two notification nodes you do not use."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "9032cfed-0278-495f-ba0d-775fcf5d86ec",
      "name": "Step 1 - Settings",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -1856,
        32
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 300,
        "height": 592,
        "content": "## 1. Settings - edit only this node\n\nEvery folder ID, the notification channel and your e-mail signature live here, so the rest of the workflow needs no editing.\n\n`attachment_file_id` is optional. Leave it empty and the draft is created without an attachment."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "6e2664aa-a3eb-4a2a-8d9d-0ffd0b2a0e9f",
      "name": "Step 2 - Fetch and read",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -1536,
        32
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 990,
        "height": 592,
        "content": "## 2. Fetch the cards and read them\n\nLists the files in the unprocessed folder, downloads each image as binary, and sends it to Gemini with a strict JSON-only prompt.\n\nThe Code node strips code fences, parses the JSON and, if that fails, regex-scans the raw text for an e-mail address, so a slightly malformed answer is still usable."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "8c88e439-2d4d-4026-962f-45bc792bca5a",
      "name": "Step 3 - Email check",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -528,
        32
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 260,
        "height": 592,
        "content": "## 3. Is the address usable?\n\nA regex decides whether the card can become a draft. Failures are not dropped: they take the lower path and are reported to the team."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "d5835fcd-084b-48e1-a986-f92a794086c0",
      "name": "Step 4 - Draft and attachment",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -256,
        32
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 1240,
        "height": 592,
        "content": "## 4. Build the draft and attach the file\n\nBuilds subject and body from your signature fields, attaches the Drive file when `attachment_file_id` is set, creates a Gmail **draft**, then files the card image in the processed folder."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "30e21cc9-264e-42cf-bda9-48d3bb26ec33",
      "name": "Manual review path",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        208,
        640
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 3,
        "width": 320,
        "height": 352,
        "content": "## Manual review path\n\nNo readable e-mail address. The Drive link is passed into the notification so a person can open the card and handle it."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "c64a785f-8616-4379-9966-e605115ce6ea",
      "name": "Step 5 - Notify the team",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        1008,
        32
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 760,
        "height": 748,
        "content": "## 5. Notify the team\n\nThe Switch reads `notify_channel` from **Settings** and runs one branch only.\n\n- **Slack** - Slack credential, channel name taken from Settings\n- **Discord** - webhook URL credential, nothing else to configure\n- **Chatwork** - HTTP Request with a Header Auth credential named X-ChatWorkToken, room ID from Settings\n\nDelete the two branches you do not need."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "d99d6a08-a202-47fd-b4db-7c3c523c153a",
      "name": "Notify Chatwork",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "notes": "Header Auth credential with the header X-ChatWorkToken",
      "onError": "continueRegularOutput",
      "position": [
        1552,
        592
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "url": "=https://api.chatwork.com/v2/rooms/{{ $('Settings').first().json.chatwork_room_id }}/messages",
        "method": "POST",
        "options": {},
        "sendBody": true,
        "contentType": "form-urlencoded",
        "authentication": "genericCredentialType",
        "bodyParameters": {
          "parameters": [
            {
              "name": "body",
              "value": "={{ $json.notify_text }}"
            },
            {
              "name": "self_unread",
              "value": "1"
            }
          ]
        },
        "genericAuthType": "httpHeaderAuth"
      },
      "credentials": {
        "httpHeaderAuth": {
          "id": "credential-id",
          "name": "Header Auth account"
        }
      },
      "notesInFlow": true,
      "typeVersion": 4.2
    }
